<Placemark>
	<name>Jaure Old Aidpost Site 2026-11-15 08:02:35</name>
	<description><![CDATA[<!-- desc_gen:start -->
<font color="black"><table width="100%"><tr><td width="100%" align="center"><a href="files/1000062832.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000062832.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br /><a href="files/1000062831.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000062831.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br />
<!-- desc_user:start -->
Also this site was Jaure's first old village. It was called "Wibi." When the population of the people were dying related to sorcery and magic practices, the people migrated to their next location "Anei." and later settled again at Jaure's current village. The name "Jaure" refers to pine trees in Jaure language.
<!-- desc_user:end -->
</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1"><hr></td></tr><tr><td><table width="100%"><tr><td align="left" valign="center"><small><b>Altitude</b></small></td><td align="center" valign="center">704 m</td></tr>
